@node MAIN "AmiCodeIDE - Manual"

@{b}AmiCodeIDE@{ub} - programming with an AI agent, right on the Amiga

AmiCodeIDE is a development environment for AmigaOS 3.2 with a built-in AI agent. You describe what a program should do - the agent writes the source, builds it with the matching compiler, reads the error messages and fixes them until it works. Everything happens on the Amiga itself; no other computer is needed.

@{b}Contents@{ub}

   @{" Introduction          " link INTRO}  What AmiCodeIDE can do
   @{" Requirements          " link REQUIRE}  What must be installed
   @{" Installation          " link INSTALL}  Copying programs and manual
   @{" Language              " link LANGUAGE}  English, German and other catalogs
   @{" First start           " link FIRSTSTART}  Your first program in five minutes
   @{" Settings              " link PREFS}  Providers, API keys and model
   @{" Appearance            " link APPEARANCE}  Light/dark, colors and fonts
   @{" New project           " link NEWPROJECT}  The project assistant
   @{" The main window       " link MAINWINDOW}  Project tree, editor, agent, build log
   @{" Working with the agent " link AGENT}  Good tasks and examples
   @{" Sessions              " link SESSIONS}  Resuming earlier conversations
   @{" Skills                " link SKILLS}  Amiga knowledge for the model
   @{" Commands              " link COMMANDS}  /help, /model, /diff, /undo ...
   @{" Approvals and safety  " link SAFETY}  Modes, questions, backups
   @{" Languages and tools   " link TOOLCHAINS}  C, BASIC, E, assembler, scripts
   @{" Internet access       " link WEB}  Searching and reading web pages
